        <body>
            <div xml:id="d451-a1">

                <pb facs="0812" n="712" sameAs="frus:frus1880/pg712"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 695.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. McPherson to Mr. Evarts.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1879-10-23"><hi rendition="#small-caps">October</hi> 23,
                            1879</date>. (Received October 24.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose herewith letter of Mr. B. M.
                    Hartshorne, a citizen of New Jersey, who is largely engaged in the Mexican
                    trade. He requests me to forward to yon the accompanying correspondence in
                    relation to what seems a great outrage on the part of the Mexican authorities,
                    and to ask if nothing can be done by way of redress. Your early attention is
                    respectfully solicited.</p>
                <p>With great respect, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>J. R. McPHERSON,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">United States Senator,
                            New Jersey.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
